[#:seon.task{:name "identities-hash-structure-not-printed-text"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "seon.id/id hashes the canonical printed text of its data (streamed into SHA-256 since f3b05eb31, so memory is constant, but time is still the printer's). Measured on default 2026-09-28 over the 2,387 test reach-digest inputs (about 600 MB printed): printing into the digest 8.7 s and 13.4 GB allocated; a tagged structural walk (type byte, UTF-8 name or string with its length, collection count, children) straight into the MessageDigest 1.55 s and 3.1 GB, unoptimized; hasch edn-hash about 35% faster than printing but allocating more. Every stored identity (definition digests, error signatures, evaluation and test ids) changes with the encoding, so it needs the owner's go and one store rebuild. Root deferred this 2026-09-28 (option 3); reach digests compose stored leaf digests per call-graph component and never print (seon.test.runner/reach-component-digests, 2026-10-07). Measured 2026-10-07: id/id's callers hash small values (917,027 calls, mean 21 us, max 23 ms; largest input found the projection's forms, 641 KB, 6.6 ms), so the encoding change buys speed only, not bounded output."
             :must-read #{seon.id/id seon.id/printed seon.test.runner/reach-component-digests}}]
